      "side": 1,
      "message": "Wouldn\u0027t it be easier to extract the \"default\" gjf version into it\u0027s own file and read that from both setup_gjf.sh and run_gjf.sh? also let run_gjf.sh take an argument.\nThen you always know which version the user wants to run and you can check explicitly for that version.\nAnother idea is to consolidate them into one script:\n```\n$ ./tools/gjf.sh run 1.22.0 # installs 1.22.0 if necessary and runs it\n$ ./tools/gjf.sh run # installs default version of gjf and runs it\n$ ./tools/gjf setup # installs default gfj\n$ ./tools/gjf setup 1.22.0 # installs 1.22.0 of gjf\n```",
